# Autonomous Magnetic Proximity Fuze Simulation for Naval Torpedo Systems


An end-to-end MATLAB simulation framework modeling the kinematics, geomagnetic field distortion, sensor dynamics, DSP filtering pipeline, and safety/detonation logic of a naval torpedo magnetic pistol.

## 1. Mathematical & Physical Principles
A moving ferromagnetic vessel (surface ship or submarine) perturbs the ambient geomagnetic background field. The torpedo's on-board magnetometer samples this dynamic vector perturbation.

### Anomaly Field Formulation

The ship's induced and permanent magnetization is modeled as a modified magnetic dipole with boundary-layer proximity, aspect angle, vessel scale, and turbulent wake corrections.

### Derivative Gradient Estimation

To capture the transition during close approach or under-keel passage, the instantaneous magnetic gradient is approximated by a 5-sample backward difference 
